      <h1 id="zero-trust-manager-monitoring_{context}" class="group scroll-mt-20">Monitoring Zero Trust Workload Identity Managergit<a href="#zero-trust-manager-monitoring_{context}" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h1>
      <p class="_abstract">Track the performance of the Zero Trust Workload Identity Manager by collecting metrics. Configure monitoring to collect metrics from the Security Production Identity Framework for Everyone (SPIRE) Server and SPIRE Agent components.</p>
      <h2 id="zero-trust-manager-enable-monitoring_zero-trust-manager-monitoring" class="group scroll-mt-20">Enabling user workload monitoring<a href="#zero-trust-manager-enable-monitoring_zero-trust-manager-monitoring" class="ml-2 text-muted-foreground opacity-0 group-hover:opacity-100 no-underline" aria-hidden="true" tabindex="-1">&para;</a></h2>
      <p class="_abstract">Enable user workload monitoring to track metrics for your user-defined projects. Configuring this feature allows you to observe application performance and helps you maintain the health of your services.</p>
      <p><strong>Prerequisites</strong></p>
      <ul><li>You have access to the cluster as a user with the <code>cluster-admin</code> cluster role.</li></ul>
      <p><strong>Procedure</strong></p>
      <ol>
      <li>
      Create the <code>cluster-monitoring-config.yaml</code> file to define and configure the <code>ConfigMap</code>:
      <CodeBlock code={"apiVersion: v1\nkind: ConfigMap\nmetadata:\n  name: cluster-monitoring-config\n  namespace: openshift-monitoring\ndata:\n  config.yaml: |\n    enableUserWorkload: true"} lang="yaml" />
      </li>
      <li>
      Apply the <code>ConfigMap</code> by running the following command:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc apply -f cluster-monitoring-config.yaml"} lang="terminal" />
      </li>
      </ol>
      <p><strong>Verification</strong></p>
      <ul>
      <li>
      Verify that the monitoring components for user workloads are running in the <code>openshift-user-workload-monitoring</code> namespace:
      <CodeBlock code={"$ oc -n openshift-user-workload-monitoring get pod"} lang="terminal" />
      <CodeBlock code={"NAME                                   READY   STATUS    RESTARTS   AGE\nprometheus-operator-6cb6bd9588-dtzxq   2/2     Running   0          50s\nprometheus-user-workload-0             6/6     Running   0          48s\nprometheus-user-workload-1             6/6     Running   0          48s\nthanos-ruler-user-workload-0           4/4     Running   0          42s\nthanos-ruler-user-workload-1           4/4     Running   0          42s"} lang="text" title="Example output" />
      </li>
      </ul>
      <p>The status of the pods such as <code>prometheus-operator</code>, <code>prometheus-user-workload</code>, and <code>thanos-ruler-user-workload</code> must be <code>Running</code>.</p>
